{"kind":"event","event_id":10930,"event_uid":"01M2S8TND2T4ZGNVH0HJQ0Y8N5","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":434,"issue_uid":"01M2S8QWQH95Q2KRSZTQQ4Y00H","issue_short_id":"y00h","actor":"impl:3@run-187","hlc_physical_ms":1789702002082,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"45a454ec6e425e29b0ff1a908a34bc0823478426d4830cb09e4ba1ad6340a981","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2S8TND1T4HDMKVNMCNAZA6M","author":"impl:3@run-187","body":"Landed as one sentence in exam.md's imports-and-calls paragraph: \"A node exam that starts a process passes `env: simEnv()`, the named export of `fleet/tests/_helpers.mjs`, and never `process.env`.\"\n\nTwo choices a later session would otherwise rediscover:\n\n- The path is written relative to the repository, not as a relative import. An unguarded exam lands at fleet/tests/exams/<run>/, two levels below fleet/tests/, so any literal ../ depth in the brief would be wrong for exams written at another depth; the examiner resolves it.\n- \"the named export of\" carries where simEnv comes from without a second occurrence of the identifier — M1 caps the file at exactly one, so the import line could not be spelled out as a second mention.\n\nAll four Run: legs green. Three role files total 866 words of the 900 budget, leaving 34 for a future sentence. Footprint is factory/roles/exam.md alone; both freeze Checks pass. No state exam in this Proof, so state.reached stays unset.","created_at":"2026-09-18T03:26:42.081439273Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-18T03:26:42.082Z"}
